{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport hashlib,json,re\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntext=Path('paper.tex').read_text()\nkeys=set(re.findall(r'@\\\\w+\\\\s*\\\\{\\\\s*([\"'^,]+)'\"',Path('references.bib').read_text()))\ncited={key.strip() for match in re.findall(r'\\\\\\\\cite\\\\w*\\\\s*\\\\{([\"'^}]+)'\"\\\\}',text) for key in match.split(',')}\nprovenance=json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())['references']\nprint('Bibliography entries:',len(keys),'unique cited keys:',len(cited))\nprint('Undefined keys:',sorted(cited-keys))\nprint('Missing provenance:',sorted(cited-{ref['citation_key'] for ref in provenance}))\nprint('Missing consulted evidence files:',[ref['citation_key'] for ref in provenance if not Path(ref['evidence_path']).is_file()])\nfor name in ['paper.tex','references.bib','references_provenance.json']:\n print('SHA256',name,hashlib.sha256(Path(name).read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nprint('\\\\nCLAIMS WITHOUT EXTERNAL CITATIONS')\nclaims=json.loads(Path('claims_grounding.json').read_text())['claims']\nfor claim in claims:\n if not claim.get('citation_keys'): print(claim['claim'])\ndata=json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\nprint('\\\\nDATA SUPPORT:', len(data['ablation_studies']),'ablations;',len(data['all_programs']),'retained programs; final evaluation keys:',list(data['final_evaluation']))\nprint('Primary metrics:',json.dumps(data['final_evaluation']['metrics'],sort_keys=True))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport hashlib,json,re\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntext=Path('paper.tex').read_text()\nkeys=set(re.findall(r'@\\\\w+\\\\s*\\\\{\\\\s*([\"'^,]+)'\"',Path('references.bib').read_text()))\ncited={key.strip() for match in re.findall(r'\\\\\\\\cite\\\\w*\\\\s*\\\\{([\"'^}]+)'\"\\\\}',text) for key in match.split(',')}\nprovenance=json.loads(Path('references_provenance.json').read_text())['references']\nprint('Bibliography entries:',len(keys),'unique cited keys:',len(cited))\nprint('Undefined keys:',sorted(cited-keys))\nprint('Missing provenance:',sorted(cited-{ref['citation_key'] for ref in provenance}))\nprint('Missing consulted evidence files:',[ref['citation_key'] for ref in provenance if not Path(ref['evidence_path']).is_file()])\nfor name in ['paper.tex','references.bib','references_provenance.json']:\n print('SHA256',name,hashlib.sha256(Path(name).read_bytes()).hexdigest())\nprint('\\\\nCLAIMS WITHOUT EXTERNAL CITATIONS')\nclaims=json.loads(Path('claims_grounding.json').read_text())['claims']\nfor claim in claims:\n if not claim.get('citation_keys'): print(claim['claim'])\ndata=json.loads(Path('paper_data.json').read_text())\nprint('\\\\nDATA SUPPORT:', len(data['ablation_studies']),'ablations;',len(data['all_programs']),'retained programs; final evaluation keys:',list(data['final_evaluation']))\nprint('Primary metrics:',json.dumps(data['final_evaluation']['metrics'],sort_keys=True))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Bibliography entries: 25 unique cited keys: 25\nUndefined keys: []\nMissing provenance: []\nMissing consulted evidence files: []\nSHA256 paper.tex f8711f1c4234ae3620cdb1ff8f09c78e9641f3243020999ff1366d21073a9e3b\nSHA256 references.bib da121db5d6947eb9e2e37d942a79286e1e7d5054c9d658798b20b93947dce04c\nSHA256 references_provenance.json db097753c2c12c8b4010d8af69df73e401bcfc3f7ce261c40fe42bb18a773f3f\n\nCLAIMS WITHOUT EXTERNAL CITATIONS\nFinal evaluation completed and qualified; qualification is not evidence of universal validity or superiority.\nThe final frozen MTEB plane has 126 rows and 135 task/subset columns, not independent benchmark suites; results revision is 6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383.\nEnglish text-only main-score extraction preserves bounded noncorrelations and maps correlations by (x+1)/2; task-definition revision 5a83aafe4e7140d0606b96f59448c704f31dbf76, global support 32 and row support 12 are manifest rules.\nHistory/test alias and normalized content separation are checked; family holdout additionally separates heuristic family labels. This does not certify true ancestry or pretraining independence.\nA shuffled approximately two-thirds reservoir, cut at least eight, is disjoint from a sealed target set fixed across budgets and methods; only observed cells are retrospectively evaluated.\nRank-four ridge ALS with ridge 0.1, fifty sweeps and Gaussian factor initialization SD 0.1 fits observed entries only; historical means remain fixed.\nRidge conditioning and the all-column integrated-variance acquisition formula describe the evaluated source. The rank-one algebra is a surrogate reduction, not an MAE or calibrated posterior guarantee; selection is independent of revealed values.\nDonor-excluded auxiliary predictions yield residuals only for observed donor targets; shared-anchor kernel weights are multiplied by overlap fraction, use a 0.025 scale floor, and vanish at zero overlap.\nWeighted median residual correction uses effective-count shrinkage, excludes queried columns, clips to [0,1], and leaves the base unchanged below total-weight threshold 1e-12 or at zero blend.\nHistory-only nested calibration uses two validation folds and two donor folds, at most 16 validation rows, 128 donors, 12 auxiliary sweeps, and pool cap min(512,max(64,floor(196608/N))).\nCalibration grid h={0.35,0.75,1.5}, tau={4,16}, alpha={0,0.25,0.5,1} includes exact zero fallback; historical finite-cell pooling differs from fixed-target outer row averaging.\nALS arithmetic cost O(E r^2+(M+N)r^3) per sweep and donor-by-column residual storage are direct algebraic consequences of the inspected dense-solve loops, not measured runtime or novel theory.\nFive final references are column mean, query mean, random-query low-rank, variance-query low-rank, and linear ridge; query policies differ and centered missing entries in linear ridge are zero-filled.\nConstant history preserves masks and replaces observed values by column means. Column shifting rolls each value/mask pair by an independent nonzero offset, preserving per-column observed multisets; controls match model holdout.\nBudgets 1,2,4,8 use nested prefixes; seeds 6841,8089,9011; history/test sizes 94/32 except final family split 93/33; six primary condition/seed averages have equal weight.\nAggregate MAE 0.040807843083862115, RMSE 0.06432104648676243, strongest aggregate baseline 0.045249969215420516, gain 0.004442126131558401, relative reduction 9.816860008%.\nAll six estimators and both holdouts in Table 1, the complete budget table, and seed table reproduce retained episode arrays; the studied configuration has lower aggregate MAE in each holdout than every reference.\nStudied MAE model/family=0.038312665669/0.043303020499 versus linear ridge 0.045116500008/0.045383438423; partitions differ, so no causal effect of family membership is inferred.\nStudied seed MAEs 0.038496586319,0.041126033629,0.042800909303 (sample SD 0.002169731091); linear-ridge seed MAEs 0.041657905965,0.045940218194,0.048151783488. Seeds share source data.\nPrimary budget MAEs 0.045233341978,0.042208509062,0.039639061083,0.036150460213 decrease over k=1,2,4,8. Each holdout seed-mean curve decreases, without per-model monotonicity or sufficient-budget claims.\nAt eight queries studied model/family errors are 0.034476748972/0.037824171454, versus ridge 0.039273276354/0.039840694780.\nPaired component resampling uses 400 draws and RNG 424242; quantiles .005/.995 for each of five baselines precede separate minima of lower and upper bounds. These are not a conventional single-comparator interval.\nReported bound minima [0.0021032442082077377,0.009199712663056218] are reconstructed exactly; all baseline-specific intervals in the supplement come from the same retained paired arrays.\nMatched model-holdout intact MAE 0.038312665669 rises to 0.064367113099 under constant history and 0.068569520893 under column shifts; shifted column mean is 0.064367113099 and variance low-rank 0.070913935972. The method loses to column mean under shifts.\nConstant-history column means and all centered historical linear references equal the studied sealed-target MAE; controls do not isolate any component.\nAll-unqueried changing-target diagnostic MAEs A/B/C/D=0.036645358811/0.042420107742/0.065275510462/0.063523296739; not a common-target comparison.\nReset replay query sequences matched and maximum absolute prediction difference was zero; diagnostics do not certify all possible leakage checks.\nNo matched final residual-off, unconditional-residual, donor-only, support-gating, temporal, cross-leaderboard or missingness-stratified result is available; sequential development does not isolate causal components.\nTwo development configurations have numeric results; one support-gating evaluation has no retained numeric performance and an unknown failure cause. It is not a measured loss.\nManifest records current CC0-1.0 evidence and Apache-2.0 metadata but absence of a results license at the pinned snapshot; historical licensing remains qualified.\n\nDATA SUPPORT: 0 ablations; 2 retained programs; final evaluation keys: ['correct', 'evaluation_evidence', 'evaluator_sha256', 'manifest_path', 'metrics', 'outcome', 'program_tree_sha256', 'results_tree_sha256', 'status', 'task_tree_sha256']\nPrimary metrics: {\"baseline_mae\": 0.045249969215420516, \"combined_score\": 0.9591921569161379, \"constant_control_mae\": 0.06436711309859705, \"correct\": 1, \"delta_best_baseline\": 0.004442126131558401, \"gain_ci_high\": 0.009199712663056218, \"gain_ci_low\": 0.0021032442082077377, \"mae\": 0.040807843083862115, \"mae_k1\": 0.04523334197776794, \"mae_k2\": 0.0422085090615931, \"mae_k4\": 0.03963906108320536, \"mae_k8\": 0.03615046021288207, \"permuted_control_mae\": 0.06856952089296987, \"reset_max_abs_delta\": 0.0, \"rmse\": 0.06432104648676243}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
